@page "/transparency"

<PageTitle>Our sourcing</PageTitle>

<section class="transparency-hero">
    <div class="transparency-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow light">Farm to cup</p>
        <h1>Transparency should be specific</h1>
        <p>Country is not traceability. We publish the producer, lot, process, import partner, and available price data for every release.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section transparency-principles">
    <article><span class="literacy-index">01</span><h2>Buy relationships</h2><p>Repeat purchasing gives producers a reason to invest in quality and gives us a reason to learn the farm beyond one exceptional sample.</p></article>
    <article><span class="literacy-index">02</span><h2>Name the chain</h2><p>Exporters and importers make specialty coffee possible. We name them rather than editing them out of the story.</p></article>
    <article><span class="literacy-index">03</span><h2>Publish what we know</h2><p>FOB and farmgate data are different. When a number is unavailable, we say so instead of filling the gap with a vague claim.</p></article>
</section>

<section class="transparency-table-section content-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">How to read our data</p>
    <h2>Four prices, four different meanings</h2>
    <dl class="definition-list">
        <div><dt>Farmgate</dt><dd>What the farmer or cooperative receives at the point of sale.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>FOB</dt><dd>The export price when coffee is loaded for international shipment.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Landed</dt><dd>FOB plus freight, insurance, warehousing, and financing.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Retail</dt><dd>The roasted product, including weight loss, labor, packaging, and operating costs.</dd></div>
    </dl>
</section>